       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 4250 mg three times daily comes to 12,750 mg/day, which is about 5 times the FDA maximum for metformin. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, given in divided doses. A dose this high carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal renal function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Some possible intended doses:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **425 mg PO TID**, which is not a standard tablet strength.\n- **500 mg or 1000 mg PO BID or TID**, within the usual range.\n\nWhat dose do you want? If you really do intend 4250 mg per dose, please confirm that explicitly and I'll reconsider. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
