     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 12,750 mg/day is about 5 times the maximum metformin dose. No indication I know of supports that dose, and it carries a high risk of severe lactic acidosis. A single 4250 mg dose would also be more than 5 of the largest tablets (850 mg). I can't enter an order that I expect to seriously harm the patient.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg PO TID with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower starting dose such as 500 mg BID with titration.\n- **Add a note for pharmacy.** If you think there's an unusual clinical reason for the higher dose, I can help you document it. Pharmacy or the clinical decision support team would need to review it before it goes through.\n- **Check for a mix-up.** The intended dose may have been a different number, or the order may be meant for another drug.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
